  "body": "What is missing: PR 1583 (the replacement for PR 773, part-orientation dropdowns) adds two user-facing undoable commands, `AlignPartCylinder` and `PlaceSetupOrigin`, with no MCP tool in `crates/app/src/mcp/`. AGENTS.md \"Commands ship with an MCP tool\" asks for the tool in the same PR or a follow-up issue named in the PR body; this is that follow-up (found by the review of PR 1583).\n\nWanted:\n- An MCP tool for each command, calling the same undoable command the GUI uses (one undo step each), with refusals by name: unknown model or setup, a pick that is not a cylinder, an axis that does not land on the target, a no-op.\n- A row for each in the camcraft-mcp skill's tool table.\n- A test per tool in `crates/app/tests/` that drives it headlessly and checks undo restores the previous pose/origin.\n\nSafety: part orientation decides which face is machined, so the tool keeps the command's own check that the axis lands on the target before anything is stored (effort floor: high).\n\nDone means: both tools are listed by `tools/list`, each has a passing headless test with undo, and the skill table names them.\n",
